  "assessments": [
    {
      "section": "14.7",
      "evidence": "ch11-http seven complete files and cached reqwest blocking API",
      "judgment": "URL components/fragment, HTTP status versus transport/request failure, 2xx policy, redirect5, proxy/direct and selected TLS feature roles are accurate. Typed stage errors preserve HTTP status for Body failure and separate process exit codes. No charset means UTF-8 replacement decoding and no body-size cap as stated. Pinned blocking ClientBuilder timeout is retained separately and supplied to send wait and response.text wait; claim is deliberately not a shared 10-second total. Normal main is synchronous. Four unit and two CLI tests are offline; two optional public URL commands have no deterministic-output or speed claim. Status-line exercise keeps 200/404 report semantics."
    },
    {
      "section": "14.8",
      "evidence": "http-single-basic six complete files, completed http-single nine files including uncompiled README, pinned reqwest async implementation",
      "judgment": "Async send is an ordinary factory and creates total timeout before polling; same timeout is passed into Response/body. Client sharing/pool, owned final_url before consuming response, elapsed boundary and u128 measurement match source. Basic package has no JSON dependency/module; completed normal library really loads fully taught reply.rs. Three core+one reply unit and two CLI tests match counts. JSON policy checks failed HTTP, then absent body, then Deserialize schema; owned title survives report scope. Artificial report/example is clearly distinguished from real HTTP."
    },
    {
      "section": "14.9 minimal and fixture",
      "evidence": "no-lib local-basic two files, local-service normal lib/main and all complete examples, normal http-single path dependency; cached axum serve/redirect",
      "judgment": "Router/get function values, tuple IntoResponse, loopback bind port0 with continuously held listener and serve IntoFuture conversion are correctly taught before selected source. WithGracefulShutdown is IntoFuture, not itself Future, and task+service result layers are checked. Complete Fixture contains every owned helper before its first command. State/Path extraction and short Mutex guard remove preserve Send across await; entered precedes headers and is distinct from ready. Option::take consumes each release sender; shutdown closes gates before signaling and awaiting server, while finish_client separately aborts+awaits client. Assertions follow owned-resource cleanup."
    },
    {
      "section": "14.9 tests and solution",
      "evidence": "seven isolated integration targets, nine total test functions, closed_gate_solution",
      "judgment": "fixed_responses tests three fixed statuses plus one redirect (hits5), loop rejection after initial+5 followed redirects (hits6), and simultaneous distinct dynamic ports. gates uses independent releases and checks no premature completion/reused/outside release. request_timeout waits real entered then pauses and resumes before cleanup; only Request/header-phase deadline is claimed. absent_entered first obtains real completed /loop result under15-second notification budget, then virtual5-second entered timeout and preserves original redirect error. client_cancel preserves hits and still shuts server. Closing unopened gate sends normal503 body before shutdown completes, not Request failure. Finite CLI stdout matches source. Each newly introduced test API/source precedes exact --test target; all-targets comes after complete source."
    }
